 {:db/id "q-15144/ma-source-field/1e2411f2e8bcae3ba96b59e76da577fe8102bef0d92b499c40459902b7c352ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "61740183-1d83-54ca-8ff3-51d0ccdbf570" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-15144/ma-source-field/1e2411f2e8bcae3ba96b59e76da577fe8102bef0d92b499c40459902b7c352ee/b0fb5bc8a1505938e2385dc7d962ebae607c545bbd401975eff437a6afea918e" "q-15144/ma-source-field/1e2411f2e8bcae3ba96b59e76da577fe8102bef0d92b499c40459902b7c352ee/9ae06f336153fe78affd5f3509f6f3dae31675f79791bd5309a1dd3f7ad5f9b7" "q-15144/ma-source-field/1e2411f2e8bcae3ba96b59e76da577fe8102bef0d92b499c40459902b7c352ee/227be46d5ac48a95a9d1881256485217c76b874d77639fff2e23567daf1ac344" "q-15144/ma-source-field/1e2411f2e8bcae3ba96b59e76da577fe8102bef0d92b499c40459902b7c352ee/5d8147b723e341f427755caf06a015a8a6d918d3ac3e1892d3c43dba7e170c59" "q-15144/ma-source-field/1e2411f2e8bcae3ba96b59e76da577fe8102bef0d92b499c40459902b7c352ee/2961c271e873a1748e46d385ea3086152679d712c26e56a4b8fca3b2daea5f74"] :answer-field/correct "q-15144/ma-source-field/1e2411f2e8bcae3ba96b59e76da577fe8102bef0d92b499c40459902b7c352ee/b0fb5bc8a1505938e2385dc7d962ebae607c545bbd401975eff437a6afea918e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "dd646452-89ff-5f38-8817-208b877e41c6"] :question/problem "![](images/4b/4b03822d65ec9f5bea3a1e47d25e4831470754fa09cef510e7c452cc292e9e40.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\theta {e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\theta {e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={e}^{\\theta }+\\theta {e}^{\\theta }=(1+\\theta ){e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(\\theta {e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{((1+\\theta ){e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}{e}^{2\\theta }+(1+2\\theta +{\\theta }^{2}){e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1){e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15144/ma-source-field/1e2411f2e8bcae3ba96b59e76da577fe8102bef0d92b499c40459902b7c352ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
