 {:db/id "q-15469/ma-source-field/3dffb30d68cbcacf09870f6e58839dfaa3a3852b4b5451fd9038dd23ecc83988" :answer-field/id #uuid "afbc7c1c-c03b-5382-bd6b-5a9beec491d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-15469/ma-source-field/3dffb30d68cbcacf09870f6e58839dfaa3a3852b4b5451fd9038dd23ecc83988/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-15469/ma-source-field/3dffb30d68cbcacf09870f6e58839dfaa3a3852b4b5451fd9038dd23ecc83988/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-15469/ma-source-field/3dffb30d68cbcacf09870f6e58839dfaa3a3852b4b5451fd9038dd23ecc83988/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-15469/ma-source-field/3dffb30d68cbcacf09870f6e58839dfaa3a3852b4b5451fd9038dd23ecc83988/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-15469/ma-source-field/3dffb30d68cbcacf09870f6e58839dfaa3a3852b4b5451fd9038dd23ecc83988/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472"] :answer-field/correct "q-15469/ma-source-field/3dffb30d68cbcacf09870f6e58839dfaa3a3852b4b5451fd9038dd23ecc83988/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-15469" :question/id #uuid "7f9e0331-ffe6-5489-b436-faf1f0bea590" :question/math-academy-id "q-15469" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{3}+1,\\,y={t}^{4}+2{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6{t}^{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4t({t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{4t({t}^{2}+1)}{6{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({t}^{2}+1)}{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2((1)^{2}+1)}{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-15469/ma-source-field/3dffb30d68cbcacf09870f6e58839dfaa3a3852b4b5451fd9038dd23ecc83988"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
