 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "846d6059-ad4f-5e01-8a65-610c7d23e3a4"] :question/problem "![](images/b9/b95c538613ee8672e0f1cac970b7af230ec40bf3075e609b1e03f7cad4382fb1.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<1,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/19/19e8e52881066864cba562ed2a8cdc2944b9dae416c7124fdee207cdad1d8bdf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/90/907e996fb7aea36e0c924feb0f5d9dc6804c768be775953d277e84b0145ef5a0.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<1,\\,-1<y<0}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158314/ma-source-field/2fba391ab4ee8859eb899709ff0daa95c5eabacdcc75866aed751ca18b7e34de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
 [:db/retract 17592186152438 :question/answer-fields 17592186149129]
