 {:db/id "q-158569" :question/id #uuid "d3d7c34b-eed1-5181-a45d-9a598cc7cc31" :question/math-academy-id "q-158569" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)={2}^{y-2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n- $y-2x$ is defined for all $x$ and $y,$ and\n\n- ${2}^{g(x,y)}$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, ${2}^{y-2x}$ is defined for all values of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the domain of $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158569/ma-source-field/6909738b71fa24539729b9ab8100ddb76dc06ce2295895092781dd5263c54a98"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
