 {:db/id "q-159764" :question/id #uuid "0bb92e93-2cdf-508a-a231-165363849a16" :question/math-academy-id "q-159764" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159764/ma-source-field/9e38a0a6a38a2f87d460086f70a43c42db678e0a6009dae64fcc8ca14f73cc48"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
