 {:db/id "q-159797" :question/id #uuid "f9f71d03-299c-533e-bd5f-2dfe8453c281" :question/math-academy-id "q-159797" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ has endpoints at $A(1,1)$ and $B(-1,2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(2,2)$ and ${B}^{′}(-5,7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159797/ma-source-field/2bbf4d28db27166df1846572a06b602124d99503ef19cf9636f039bcc3958add"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
