 {:db/id "q-160013" :question/id #uuid "78111624-f670-5df8-b6e2-bb5a5dde19ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-160013" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{3}{4}+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$, calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\frac{3}{4}$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160013/ma-source-field/07cb960c24a71e00092e13a425913d4f325a04212271517051fe964e45e1d1dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
