 {:db/id "q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41/fd37b031ab84bfb8ec8eb3bb90ac8fcf4bf0d2a39fa13a91238360a7ae98a273" :answer/id #uuid "14c27fbe-cfe3-5924-a55c-3737ccd260a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the line $v=\\frac{3}{2}u.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41/db461dec809acacd1d9eed8256b39bc67ffb2406794a2c89bc30a491c2461de6" :answer/id #uuid "1b3464e3-f53d-53d8-877c-0141084f3eb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabola $2v=3{u}^{2}.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41" :answer-field/id #uuid "753118cd-0a71-5bb3-aaee-283497ceb3e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41/ab63356239e33d80c4882ec5be3dd5ed56752b67af5174b433b1b3d857f97e58" "q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41/8f386933185d00fbff379b5664c988026c52ffb188eee3e8fa91182ebdb5d28a" "q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41/159049bbdc812c6c7d3f5e556d3556d018fdd397f09b829c6d1d5633329f8f23" "q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41/fd37b031ab84bfb8ec8eb3bb90ac8fcf4bf0d2a39fa13a91238360a7ae98a273" "q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41/db461dec809acacd1d9eed8256b39bc67ffb2406794a2c89bc30a491c2461de6"] :answer-field/correct "q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41/fd37b031ab84bfb8ec8eb3bb90ac8fcf4bf0d2a39fa13a91238360a7ae98a273" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-160473" :question/id #uuid "f05de000-4a38-5b78-b8b6-ab15cb5a35af" :question/math-academy-id "q-160473" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3{u}^{2}+2{v}^{2} \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=3{u}^{2}+2{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=u+v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =6u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =4v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6u & 4v \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6u\\cdot 1-4v\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6u-4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 6u-4v & =0 \\\\ v & =\\frac{3}{2}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v=\\frac{3}{2}u$ defines a line in the $uv$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160473/ma-source-field/d0e28d1fb67d5290b2e44c0ee9a6e59afd01e29b552bba1800fca2678f5dea41"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
