 {:db/id "q-160711/ma-source-field/5cff4e3ecee1a83fe8b8f83c1c5c2aa91709f2f1fb4acc92dbf51c4efa52ad46" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5472ad-00ad-5af8-bfaf-97021ee46355" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-160711/ma-source-field/5cff4e3ecee1a83fe8b8f83c1c5c2aa91709f2f1fb4acc92dbf51c4efa52ad46/a057373cff28314c66ffa64a0efeffca3311a7906e238c4cdceaa0678a1dfacd" "q-160711/ma-source-field/5cff4e3ecee1a83fe8b8f83c1c5c2aa91709f2f1fb4acc92dbf51c4efa52ad46/d92eaee14f04749e4845b51824ebf32a4720933dde8a7ff5d34873421df2e08f" "q-160711/ma-source-field/5cff4e3ecee1a83fe8b8f83c1c5c2aa91709f2f1fb4acc92dbf51c4efa52ad46/3cdd66486a32ae11d1d881fd0e525032b1d87822d2d73f4811442e4f725239d6" "q-160711/ma-source-field/5cff4e3ecee1a83fe8b8f83c1c5c2aa91709f2f1fb4acc92dbf51c4efa52ad46/42d109bdc40646239c04bba8fee40aa919a23194fe8104009e5b95dd2deadfa5" "q-160711/ma-source-field/5cff4e3ecee1a83fe8b8f83c1c5c2aa91709f2f1fb4acc92dbf51c4efa52ad46/f6b4b63c1a6a148bae56a3091ae2e416aa25c6e114268a3021e9d9ee2f31e428"] :answer-field/correct "q-160711/ma-source-field/5cff4e3ecee1a83fe8b8f83c1c5c2aa91709f2f1fb4acc92dbf51c4efa52ad46/f6b4b63c1a6a148bae56a3091ae2e416aa25c6e114268a3021e9d9ee2f31e428" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "25e44fde-444d-5880-ba2e-43dd4bc039db"] :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xyz$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 1 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 1 & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-v)^{2}+(-u)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xyz)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =u\\cdot v\\cdot uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160711/ma-source-field/5cff4e3ecee1a83fe8b8f83c1c5c2aa91709f2f1fb4acc92dbf51c4efa52ad46"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
