 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "7492e5fe-6cc9-5d4b-8d1f-20d212147cee"] :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with normal vector $\\overset{~}{n},$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,y,\\,x⟩\\,,\\,\\overset{~}{n}(x,y,z)=⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩\\,,\\,n=\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}\\frac{\\boxed{}}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nTo compute the above dot product, we must normalize the vector $\\overset{~}{n}.$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{(2y)^{2}+(-z)^{2}+(2x)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+4{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨z,\\,y,\\,x⟩\\cdot \\frac{⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨z,\\,y,\\,x⟩\\cdot ⟨2y,\\,-z,\\,2x⟩}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2yz-yz+2{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+yz}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}+yz}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160838/ma-source-field/353d2fa8f8b5ed023b5be8a50f6af7bbbcb405a6121a56413d544e68c8f3d17a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
