 {:db/id "q-161314/ma-source-field/7f7bb250cbae6683289a559c890c41f788eaf8f09f6f649819b8c117e2d0bf27" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb2d063b-2ed3-5177-a74e-32306bee1975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161314/ma-source-field/7f7bb250cbae6683289a559c890c41f788eaf8f09f6f649819b8c117e2d0bf27/e4d92fba2aafdfc3c9e82272c51df51a3d450409dcde87e81478769a4d0b583f" "q-161314/ma-source-field/7f7bb250cbae6683289a559c890c41f788eaf8f09f6f649819b8c117e2d0bf27/731d81c50e6ff5c9701d3806fbe99a1a7bf91bea7df13eec818d5a6c93d770ad" "q-161314/ma-source-field/7f7bb250cbae6683289a559c890c41f788eaf8f09f6f649819b8c117e2d0bf27/ba447814f6c9c26bad0985dfb9b1cfe7471db81e108ffc582c1a3edb06c8cbbd" "q-161314/ma-source-field/7f7bb250cbae6683289a559c890c41f788eaf8f09f6f649819b8c117e2d0bf27/55c53fa9fe45f9c62b77a29bb646d575ce5d97a8fd408f6553ca30869eee70aa" "q-161314/ma-source-field/7f7bb250cbae6683289a559c890c41f788eaf8f09f6f649819b8c117e2d0bf27/c734ed1bda080369697543ca9102de2b0a109396523bb5452a74d3b7b476da69"] :answer-field/correct "q-161314/ma-source-field/7f7bb250cbae6683289a559c890c41f788eaf8f09f6f649819b8c117e2d0bf27/c734ed1bda080369697543ca9102de2b0a109396523bb5452a74d3b7b476da69" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161314" :question/id #uuid "d8e5c369-0d01-5527-87a6-9d6d08f8cf0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161314" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}yz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-x+y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x+y)=-1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x+y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(-1)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,{x}^{2}y(-x+y)\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{3}(-{x}^{3}y+{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161314/ma-source-field/7f7bb250cbae6683289a559c890c41f788eaf8f09f6f649819b8c117e2d0bf27"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
