 {:db/id "q-161320/ma-source-field/1a3637775e8ca10fbcc3daac23ee43fc6def96283fd7992a2fe08753a41ebef5" :answer-field/id #uuid "63dd6eb1-0216-5ca0-946f-dc8a7cfe578a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161320/ma-source-field/1a3637775e8ca10fbcc3daac23ee43fc6def96283fd7992a2fe08753a41ebef5/ba7bda6e8d43845d327f22f6fdf1207ebe7bbc92050a57ea052b2121cbe52b59" "q-161320/ma-source-field/1a3637775e8ca10fbcc3daac23ee43fc6def96283fd7992a2fe08753a41ebef5/b7e60212c81951dd091c1ab679b495c5c65b325332d38c4447c12bc4c001ef52" "q-161320/ma-source-field/1a3637775e8ca10fbcc3daac23ee43fc6def96283fd7992a2fe08753a41ebef5/072da5b355e7323099b093cfb7abbc7c77a7bed3c7d25a415b2219f196ed535a" "q-161320/ma-source-field/1a3637775e8ca10fbcc3daac23ee43fc6def96283fd7992a2fe08753a41ebef5/a05c878495f5fd1cec5aec1bfd03a14d72d05bec60e4d0fc65175893608fe76a" "q-161320/ma-source-field/1a3637775e8ca10fbcc3daac23ee43fc6def96283fd7992a2fe08753a41ebef5/de70e9586d24f4531de7aead9eca871c1661378aaf558c80bde4b8a3ba0e97f0"] :answer-field/correct "q-161320/ma-source-field/1a3637775e8ca10fbcc3daac23ee43fc6def96283fd7992a2fe08753a41ebef5/b7e60212c81951dd091c1ab679b495c5c65b325332d38c4447c12bc4c001ef52" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161320" :question/id #uuid "b5d98cd9-310e-5d64-ad53-16fad07f2de6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161320" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}z,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2x,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(-2x)}^{2}+{(-2y)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(-{x}^{4}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{4})\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161320/ma-source-field/1a3637775e8ca10fbcc3daac23ee43fc6def96283fd7992a2fe08753a41ebef5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
