 {:db/id "q-161457/ma-source-field/f9cf7be72e7027bdd14149a0b3733a0abb12259f4205cd0948967515b9cb6cd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee6b27a-bcd5-52e8-9493-e839011ba707" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161457/ma-source-field/f9cf7be72e7027bdd14149a0b3733a0abb12259f4205cd0948967515b9cb6cd9/70f3ed2f61065687b3dadd09142dd17814d767fb0778988db8bbd479dd12cce2" "q-161457/ma-source-field/f9cf7be72e7027bdd14149a0b3733a0abb12259f4205cd0948967515b9cb6cd9/970233da9fd2fbe63609692d03590c6ee31fe66a1c7892ba2ef6b9554e07a631" "q-161457/ma-source-field/f9cf7be72e7027bdd14149a0b3733a0abb12259f4205cd0948967515b9cb6cd9/963504c384925fae401c20325d6918283d9ede788226f350ccc71da4001251bc" "q-161457/ma-source-field/f9cf7be72e7027bdd14149a0b3733a0abb12259f4205cd0948967515b9cb6cd9/e83b7199a7a0e2aa22a80ed4ecfb5cde148e07704adc4cb7622ad2c977cfad95" "q-161457/ma-source-field/f9cf7be72e7027bdd14149a0b3733a0abb12259f4205cd0948967515b9cb6cd9/7dbd4c35b90a891ca8ffb8ffc7827126a9fe5e10d2050757754098a58d83a410"] :answer-field/correct "q-161457/ma-source-field/f9cf7be72e7027bdd14149a0b3733a0abb12259f4205cd0948967515b9cb6cd9/e83b7199a7a0e2aa22a80ed4ecfb5cde148e07704adc4cb7622ad2c977cfad95" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161457" :question/id #uuid "417f7e3b-659c-5f7d-913c-decf384148f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161457" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{}{∂x}-\\frac{∂g}{}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161457/ma-source-field/f9cf7be72e7027bdd14149a0b3733a0abb12259f4205cd0948967515b9cb6cd9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
