 {:db/id "q-161814/ma-source-field/1475d4e1d2dfb0a1115289bfecf6a43dc55a1027da059425661aedb45cdb866b" :answer-field/id #uuid "65676948-b2fa-585d-8619-ca89f50c6f34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161814/ma-source-field/1475d4e1d2dfb0a1115289bfecf6a43dc55a1027da059425661aedb45cdb866b/95fb92f7f41cee9638f200fbc8acf53d8597c94c84f105b35bb7763615deae67" "q-161814/ma-source-field/1475d4e1d2dfb0a1115289bfecf6a43dc55a1027da059425661aedb45cdb866b/2a24870be5f4d397a6e7f672e179c9c43aa0cef6baed112e0ba053fa458544d5" "q-161814/ma-source-field/1475d4e1d2dfb0a1115289bfecf6a43dc55a1027da059425661aedb45cdb866b/85dade9b5113e303a29d0a853feb8a933a9365abc2e1dfb4e1dd8dca4cbf2213" "q-161814/ma-source-field/1475d4e1d2dfb0a1115289bfecf6a43dc55a1027da059425661aedb45cdb866b/0868cce687771df2ff191e38962e0c53440e6db9a81dbefde5f9e9a80966c03e" "q-161814/ma-source-field/1475d4e1d2dfb0a1115289bfecf6a43dc55a1027da059425661aedb45cdb866b/eb70d249f8ef215283e1309928ce26ccc070c591a1666f43a7e7ea77d886c896"] :answer-field/correct "q-161814/ma-source-field/1475d4e1d2dfb0a1115289bfecf6a43dc55a1027da059425661aedb45cdb866b/eb70d249f8ef215283e1309928ce26ccc070c591a1666f43a7e7ea77d886c896" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161814" :question/id #uuid "d8752c18-2285-5bd2-a3b2-ba4d0420bd04" :question/math-academy-id "q-161814" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+2w \\\\ v-u \\\\ uw\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+2w,\\,y(u,v,w)=v-u,\\,z(u,v,w)=uw.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ w & 0 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ w & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(u-0)+2(0-w) \\\\  & =u-2w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ u-2w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u-2w=0$ defines the plane $u=2w.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161814/ma-source-field/1475d4e1d2dfb0a1115289bfecf6a43dc55a1027da059425661aedb45cdb866b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
